issue.description:
Remove the remaining Sidebar token status helper copy so the toggle row has no explanatory/status text in either state.

Background:
<issue id="36798378-caec-4b9e-8f4c-d11a84837552" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-93/polish-sidebar-token-toggle-spacing-and-label-styling">PUI-93</issue> correctly removed the helper note when "Use sidebar tokens" is OFF, but the ON state still renders:
"Sidebar tokens are active."

Owner direction:

* Remove the ON-state helper/status note as well.
* Do not show any helper/status text beneath the "Use sidebar tokens" toggle, regardless of whether the toggle is ON or OFF.

Target behavior:

OFF:

* show only the toggle row;
* no "Sidebar tokens are currently not applied." note.

ON:

* show only the toggle row;
* no "Sidebar tokens are active." note.

The section should visually read as:

SIDEBAR

\[toggle\] Use sidebar tokens

Background
...

Preserve:

* existing useDedicatedTokens behavior;
* sidebar token application semantics;
* persistence;
* token field visibility and ordering;
* keyboard/focus behavior;
* light/dark behavior;
* the smaller muted-foreground label styling from <issue id="36798378-caec-4b9e-8f4c-d11a84837552" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-93/polish-sidebar-token-toggle-spacing-and-label-styling">PUI-93</issue>;
* spacing between the SIDEBAR collapsible trigger and toggle row.

Do not:

* change sidebar token architecture;
* change token values;
* hide or disable the sidebar token fields;
* add replacement helper copy;
* change the Switch component itself;
* alter unrelated sidebar controls.

Acceptance:

* No helper/status note appears when Sidebar tokens are OFF.
* No helper/status note appears when Sidebar tokens are ON.
* "Sidebar tokens are active." is removed.
* The toggle continues to correctly enable/disable dedicated sidebar token application.
* Token fields remain visible and editable as before.
* No accessibility, persistence, or styling regression.
